I was just thinking that most good advertising slogans appeal to the
visual centers of the brain.  Think about it.  To get people's attention
you usually don't appeal to the left half of the brain.  Yes the
engineer in you is just amazed when we read bonnie or iozone stats, but
slogans are call forth visuals, and easy concepts.

Think about it.  A t-shirt that has iozone stats on it versus one that
has a picture of a hard drive platter burning rubber like a
high-performance tire.  Which one appeals to you emotionally?  Which one
indicates speed better to the emotional mind?

'Reise to a new level!'

